sentences.l:
Clothes, indeed, for the stranger, in a well-polished chest
lie, and gold much-wrought, and all the other
gifts, as many as the counsel-bearers of the Phaeacians have brought here;

They, to lie down going, each one went to his own house;
and when early-born appeared, rose-fingered Dawn,
to the ship they hurried, and carried the bronze good-for-men.

But Odysseus
many times toward the sun his head turned, the all-shining one,
eager for it to set;

for already is accomplished what my dear heart wished,
an escort and dear gifts, which may the gods, the children of Heaven,
make prosperous;

So having spoken, over the threshold stepped heavenly Odysseus,
and with him the herald sent forth the strength of Alcinous,
to lead the way to the swift ship and the shore of the sea;

And Arete sent with him maidservants, women,
one, a cloak well-washed having, and a tunic,
and the second a solid chest gave along to carry;

But when then they had come down to the ship and the sea,
at once these things in the hollow ship the noble escorts
receiving put away, drink and food, all of it;

And down for Odysseus they spread a blanket and a linen cloth
on the decking of the hollow ship, so that he might sleep unwaking,
at the stern;

And two for it doors there are,
the one toward the North Wind, to be gone down by, for men,
the other toward the South Wind, more divine;
